WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.170
An ancient verse warns that
pain follows an evil thought,

2
00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:08.240
as the wheel follows the foot of
the ox that draws the carriage.

3
00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:12.010
For Buddhists, every intentional
action plants a seed,

4
00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:15.050
and its fruit ripens later: in this life,

5
00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:16.670
or in another.

6
00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:20.420
But the Buddha also taught
that there is no lasting self.

7
00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:23.090
No soul moves into a new body.

8
00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:27.590
So if there is no soul,
what exactly gets reborn?

9
00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:32.090
In this mission, you'll see why
Buddhists say karma is about intention,

10
00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:33.850
not just what happens.

11
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:38.970
Then you'll face King Milinda's puzzle:
is the one reborn the same person, or

12
00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:40.130
another?

13
00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:43.920
Your mission: explain what
carries on from life to life,

14
00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:45.090
if not a soul.
